experiment: axisear
  the question      §41 run 2a. The larynx commands seven independent
                    axes; does the AIR carry them? Until v83 the renderer
                    had two resonators and `bw = 90.0f` hardcoded, so f3
                    and the three bandwidths reached no ear at all.
  the ruler         cepstral d', unbiased, through the creature's OWN
                    cochlea. d' = 1 is ~76% correct in a 2AFC, which is a
                    bar about ears rather than about classifiers.
  the anchor        F1, which the ear demonstrably resolves, at F1's own
                    reach. Every axis is also reported as a FRACTION of it.
  the dose          the SAME posture pairs at gains 0 (shipped) and 1.
                    A flat f3 column at gain 0 and a live one at gain 1 is
                    the dose-response that proves the renderer change took.

  RENDER GAINS  render_f3_gain 0.0   render_bw_gain 0.0   <- THE SHIPPED CREATURE
    f0      221.0 vs   270.8 Hz (reach   49.8, jitter sd   9.1)   d'  51.897
    f1      567.5 vs   685.5 Hz (reach  118.0, jitter sd  21.7)   d'  44.822
    f2     1519.4 vs  1819.8 Hz (reach  300.3, jitter sd  57.8)   d'  91.805
    f3     2486.2 vs  2741.1 Hz (reach  254.9, jitter sd  47.6)   d'   0.002
    bw1     132.4 vs   164.0 Hz (reach   31.6, jitter sd   5.3)   d'  -0.043
    bw2     134.5 vs   166.7 Hz (reach   32.1, jitter sd   6.0)   d'  -0.042
    bw3     134.2 vs   166.0 Hz (reach   31.8, jitter sd   5.6)   d'   0.036

  RENDER GAINS  render_f3_gain 1.0   render_bw_gain 1.0
    f0      221.0 vs   270.8 Hz (reach   49.8, jitter sd   9.1)   d'  69.070
    f1      567.5 vs   685.5 Hz (reach  118.0, jitter sd  21.7)   d'  36.398
    f2     1519.4 vs  1819.8 Hz (reach  300.3, jitter sd  57.8)   d'  94.569
    f3     2486.2 vs  2741.1 Hz (reach  254.9, jitter sd  47.6)   d'  31.195
    bw1     132.4 vs   164.0 Hz (reach   31.6, jitter sd   5.3)   d'   0.399
    bw2     134.5 vs   166.7 Hz (reach   32.1, jitter sd   6.0)   d'   0.418
    bw3     134.2 vs   166.0 Hz (reach   31.8, jitter sd   5.6)   d'   0.367

  CLAUSE 1 -- THE DOSE, against the estimator's own null floor d' = 0.346
  (= sqrt(d*(1/n0+1/n1)), derived, n = 200 per class). Required of f3, which
  is the axis the third resonator adds; bw3 is that resonator's OWN width and
  so has nothing to act on at f3_gain 0, which §41 did not notice.
    f3    gain 0 d'    0.002  ->  gain 1 d'   31.195   delta   31.193   MOVED
    bw1   gain 0 d'   -0.043  ->  gain 1 d'    0.399   delta    0.441   MOVED
    bw2   gain 0 d'   -0.042  ->  gain 1 d'    0.418   delta    0.460   MOVED
    bw3   gain 0 d'    0.036  ->  gain 1 d'    0.367   delta    0.331   flat (not required of a bandwidth)

  CLAUSE 2 -- THE POSITIVE CONTROL: the ear demonstrably resolves f1 and
  f2, so both must clear the 2AFC bar at BOTH gain settings or the ruler is
  wrong. (§41's extra demand that they not MOVE with the gain is withdrawn:
  bw1 and bw2 ARE the f1/f2 resonators' bandwidths, so render_bw_gain moves
  them by design. The first build voided here and was right to.)
    f1  d' 44.822 -> 36.398     f2  d' 91.805 -> 94.569   -> OK

  CLAUSE 3 -- THE TEST: each axis at gain 1, as a fraction of F1's d'.
  Bar: d' >= 1.0 (~76% in a 2AFC) AND clear of the 0.346 null floor, because
  a 2AFC bar beneath the estimator's own noise is not a bar.
    f1    d'   36.398    1.000 x F1   -> AUDIBLE
    f2    d'   94.569    2.598 x F1   -> AUDIBLE
    f3    d'   31.195    0.857 x F1   -> AUDIBLE
    bw1   d'    0.399    0.011 x F1   -> below the bar
    bw2   d'    0.418    0.011 x F1   -> below the bar
    bw3   d'    0.367    0.010 x F1   -> below the bar

  1 OF THE FOUR NEW AXES ARE AUDIBLE at their own reach, so the air
  carries them and stage 2b -- whether the auditory MODULE represents
  them -- is worth building. STILL NOT A WORD COUNT: this says the
  distinction survives the cochlea, not that the creature uses it, and
  kVLScoreFormant still scores only F1/F2.
